Tung Wah College
Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320). Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society.
With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering six professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists, diagnostic radiographer, therapeutic radiographer and physiotherapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals.
Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 20 doctoral degree, bachelor degree, sub-degree, diploma and certificate programmes in various disciplines. It has a student population of around 5,000 in 2025/2026 and nurtured more than 7,200 graduates since its inception in 2010.
Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term. It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years. To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post:
Duties and Responsibilities
The appointee will be required but not limited to:
monitor day-to-day facilities management operations;
supervise and evaluate the performance of cleaning, security, catering and landscape service providers;
conduct regular meetings with service providers for performance reviews;
handle venue booking and liaise with users;
arrange logistic and other supports to College’s events and activities;
handle car parking, warehouse management, key management, recycling, lockers/cabinets, lost & found, queries and complaints;
provide support and solutions to users;
assist in the procurement / tendering exercises ; and
work on irregular hours including Saturdays, Sundays and Public Holidays if needed.
Qualifications and Experience Required
Applicants should:
possess a Bachelor’s degree in Property Management / Facilities Management or other related disciplines;
have at least 3 years of relevant working experience in property management / facilities management, preferably gained in tertiary educational institutions;
have good organizational and communications skills;
have strong sense of responsibility, able to work under pressure and multi-tasking;
have excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, proficiency in Putonghua will be an advantage; and
be literacy in computer applications.
Application
Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience.
To apply, please submit your application via system. The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post. Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618.
Application Deadline: Until the position is filled
All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk .
